{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And he made heavy his heart.</b> It is a verbal noun (פָּעוֹל) form, like ״הָלוֹךְ וְנָסוֹעַ״ (Genesis 12), and similarly ״וְהַכּוֹת אֶת מוֹאָב״ (II Kings 3:24), ״וְשָׁאוֹל לוֹ בֵאלֹהִים״ (I Samuel 22:13), ״הַכֵּה וּפָצֹעַ״ (I Kings 20)." "<b>As YHWH had spoken.</b> And where did He speak? [Where He said,] ״and Pharaoh will not heed you.״"], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "Rashi cites each of these forms, where a verb with a prefixed vav plus ha + patach functions as an infinitive construct in the pa'al (Qal) binyan; the label פָּעוֹל denotes this infinitive usage.", 1 "Rashi supplies the implied reference to Exodus 7:4 (or 7:2), where HaShem tells Moshe that Pharaoh will not listen, which is the 'speaking' this verse points back to."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:07.861841808Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}